 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "In this opening scene of episode nine, Ivan Samsonov and his wife Nina are in bed late at night arguing about his behavior at the political concert. Furious at rumors of infidelity, Samsonov insists he did nothing wrong and angrily threatens her with divorce, while Nina laughs off his dramatic threats. Let's listen to the scene in Russian first; don't worry about catching every word.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Сколько раз тебе говорить?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Я просто сходил на концерт.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Я был там с одноклассником.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Я тебе не изменял!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nina",
   "t": "А люди говорят другое.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Мне всё равно, что ты думаешь!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Ты меня поняла?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Я разведусь с тобой!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Тебе всё понятно?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nina",
   "t": "Самсон, ну всё, хватит.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nina",
   "t": "Не смеши меня, пожалуйста.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nina",
   "t": "Пойдём уже спать.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Посмотрим, Нина. Посмотрим.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Now let's examine Ivan and Nina's midnight bedroom argument line by line. Ivan sits up in bed frowning in the dark.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Сколько раз тебе говорить?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'How many times do I have to tell you?' Samsonov expresses exasperation.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Я просто сходил на концерт.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I just went to a concert.' The past masculine verb combines with the adverb for 'simply' or 'just'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Я был там с одноклассником.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I was there with a classmate.' Notice the 'with/as' form following the preposition for 'with'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Я тебе не изменял!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I didn't cheat on you!' The verb for 'to be unfaithful' takes the 'to/for' form in standard Russian.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nina",
   "t": "А люди говорят другое.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And people say otherwise.' Nina remains skeptical about his late-night whereabouts.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Мне всё равно, что ты думаешь!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I don't care what you think!' The idiom with the 'to me/you' pronoun literally means 'to me it is all the same'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Ты меня поняла?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Did you understand me?' A short past tense question checking whether she heard him.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Я разведусь с тобой!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I will divorce you!' This phrase indicates an intention to dissolve the marriage.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Тебе всё понятно?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Is everything clear to you?' Samsonov demands acknowledgment.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nina",
   "t": "Самсон, ну всё, хватит.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Samson, that's enough, stop it.' Nina dismisses his threat with a soothing particle combination.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nina",
   "t": "Не смеши меня, пожалуйста.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Don't make me laugh, please.' This phrase urges him not to act ridiculous.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nina",
   "t": "Пойдём уже спать.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Let's just go to sleep.' Nina tries to defuse the midnight argument and turn off the light.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Посмотрим, Нина. Посмотрим.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'We will see, Nina. We will see.' Samsonov repeats the future plural verb as a stubborn final warning. Now let's listen to the entire bedroom argument again without interruption.",
